import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
CASES={
 'long-gap':('Five turns since the last drink','The original leaves the potion unused. The correction drinks one, heals 60 HP and clears confusion.'),
 'first-use':('No previous drink; turn 100','The original treats never having drunk a potion as a long delay. The correction allows this first drink.'),
 'recent':('One turn since the last drink: tradeoff','The correction conserves one potion, but stays at 321 HP and remains confused on this call. The original drinks and heals. This is not uniformly safer.'),
 'boundary-four':('Four turns since the last drink: tradeoff','Four turns is still within the repeat-drink hesitation window. The correction saves a potion, but leaves this call without healing or a confusion cure.'),
 'first-turn':('Control: first drink at internal turn 1','Original and full correction allow the first drink. Merely reversing the comparison blocks it because zero means no previous drink.'),
 'same-turn':('Control: two requests at the same clock value','The existing zero-elapsed-time exclusion is preserved. Both versions drink.'),
 'bypass-control':('Control: emergency caller bypasses hesitation','A caller explicitly asks to bypass conservation checks. Every version drinks.'),
 'reserve-control':('Control: only one potion remains','The existing reserve rule rejects use of the last potion. Every version conserves it.'),
 'empty-control':('Control: no potion remains','Every version queues no drink when the inventory contains none.')}
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','simple','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text();frames=[json.loads(l[6:]) for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith('FRAME ')]
  assert len(frames)==2
  match=re.search(r'OUTCOME (.*)',raw);outcome={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])}
  assert frames[1]['hp']-frames[0]['hp']==outcome['healed']
  assert frames[0]['potions']-frames[1]['potions']==outcome['potions_spent']
  item[phase]={'frames':frames,'outcome':outcome,'raw':raw}
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Healing-potion hesitation at the wrong time</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f5f2eb;color:#263739;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.hp{font-size:40px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native potion use · original, simple reversal and complete correction</p><h1>The Borg hesitates to drink a healing potion after the wrong delay</h1><p>A wounded, confused Warrior has seven Cure Critical Wounds potions and last drank one five Borg turns ago. The original leaves them unused, stays at 321 HP and remains confused. The correction drinks one potion, heals to 381 HP and clears confusion.</p><p>The correction conserves a potion just after a recent drink instead. That leaves the recent-drink example wounded and confused on this call: a resource tradeoff, not an overall survival improvement.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><label for="variant">Compare the original with:</label><br><select id="variant"><option value="after">Complete correction</option><option value="simple">Simple comparison reversal only</option></select><br><button data-step="0">Start</button><button data-step="1">Show potion decision</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2 id="variant-title"></h2><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>Why a simple reversal is insufficient</h2><p>The original passes 5 of 9 cases; reversing the comparison passes 8. That simple change blocks the first-ever drink at internal turn 1: zero is the stored value for no previous drink, not a real previous drink. Checking that a previous drink exists passes all 9 cases and preserves five complete control logs.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior level 40, depth 30, seed 1000, known potions. The test establishes a real earlier drink and applies controlled injuries/confusion. It advances the Borg's internal decision clock directly to isolate the elapsed-time check; it does not simulate intervening world turns or combat. Every source version uses the same setup and seed, with no RNG reset between decisions. The native potion handler computes the healing and cure and removes the actual potion.</p><p>This tests the shared potion-use helper, not the entire healing/escape decision loop. Emergency callers can bypass the hesitation rule; that path is tested unchanged. It does not prove an extra enemy attack, death, encounter frequency or that conserving a potion is always safer. The random hesitation remains probabilistic, and the result shown is one unchanged seeded experiment.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Compared</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/77">issue77 / CBUG-0061</a>. Discovery credit: borg-rs.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario'),variant=document.getElementById('variant');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;document.getElementById('variant-title').textContent=variant.options[variant.selectedIndex].text;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared',variant.value]]){let d=c[phase],f=d.frames[step],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.hp').textContent=`${f.hp} / ${f.max_hp} HP`;p.querySelector('.stats').textContent=`Healing potions: ${f.potions}. Confusion: ${f.confused>0?'present':'cleared'}.`;p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===0?'Before this potion-use request.':d.outcome.used?`Drinks one potion: heals ${d.outcome.healed} HP and clears confusion.`:'No drink requested: health and confusion remain unchanged.';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}let a=c.before.outcome,b=c[variant.value].outcome;document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=['recent','boundary-four'].includes(select.value)?'Tradeoff: correction saves one potion, but leaves 60 HP unhealed and confusion present on this call.':variant.value==='simple'&&select.value==='first-turn'?'The simple reversal wrongly rejects the first-ever drink.':a.used===b.used?'Unchanged control: same potion use, healing and confusion result.':`Recorded health: ${a.hp_after} → ${b.hp_after} HP; the correction drinks the available potion.`;for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});variant.addEventListener('change',draw);for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
